Below is a minimal example of a rotating card that flips when you hover over it.  
It uses only HTML and CSS (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
  /* Container that holds the card */
  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives a 3‑D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
  }

  /* The card itself */
  .card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Allows children to be positioned in 3‑D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Front side of the card */
  .card .front,
  .card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide the back side when facing away */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  }

  .card .front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .card .back {
    background: #f8f8f8;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Position back side behind front */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #555;
  }

  /* Rotate the card on hover */
  .card-wrapper:hover .card {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 1000px;` which gives depth to the 3‑D rotation.
2. **3‑D transform** – The `.card` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children can be positioned in 3‑D space.
3. **Backface visibility** – `backface-visibility: hidden;` hides the side that is turned away from the viewer.
4. **Rotation** – On hover, the card is rotated 180° around the Y‑axis, flipping it to show the back side.

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside the `.front` and `.back` divs to suit your design.
